--TEST--
Every one of `Core\Db\Row`'s eleven typed readers answers `?T`, so a NULL column is dealt with at the read rather than at the first use — `rule:core-classes/db-column-types`, spec § 18
--FILE--
<?nvs
// One question asked of all fourteen members at once: what does a reader
// answer when the column it names is NULL? The answer has to be the *same* for
// every one of them, because a reader that answered `T` would be a member
// where a NULL column is discovered somewhere else entirely — which is what
// `fetch`'s `false`, `null` and `""` did between them in PHP.
var $db = Core\Db::connect("main");

// A `tainted` column name is accepted everywhere a name is taken: a label is a
// lookup key, so what comes back carries the qualifiers `rule:core-classes/db-column-types` gives the
// *column* and never the ones the name arrived with.
tainted string $outside = "owner";

foreach ($db->query("select * from accounts", [])->all() as Core\Db\Row $row) {
    // The associative reading, and the only one — there is no numeric or
    // object fetch mode to ask for instead.
    bool $present = $row->has($outside);
    mixed $any = $row->get("owner");
    array<mixed> $whole = $row->toArray();

    // The eleven, in § 18's own order. A `null` from one of these is a NULL
    // column and never "no such column": that second question is `has`, above,
    // and an unknown name throws here rather than reading as absent.
    ?tainted string $owner = $row->string("owner");
    ?tainted bytes $photo = $row->bytes("photo");
    ?int $id = $row->int("id");
    ?uint $seq = $row->uint("seq");
    ?float $ratio = $row->float("ratio");
    ?bool $active = $row->bool("active");
    ?decimal $balance = $row->decimal("balance");
    ?Core\Time\Instant $seen = $row->instant("seen_at");
    ?Core\Time\Date $born = $row->date("born_on");
    ?Core\Time\TimeOfDay $opens = $row->time("opens_at");
    ?Core\Uuid $external = $row->uuid("external_id");
}

// The `Rows` half of the same sweep, so that the one refusal below is the only
// thing in this case that does not compile.
var $rows = $db->query("select id from accounts", []);
array<Core\Db\Row> $all = $rows->all();
?Core\Db\Row $first = $rows->first();
mixed $one = $rows->value();
array<mixed> $ids = $rows->column("id");
uint $count = $rows->count();

// And the bound, on a row that is not in doubt: the reader answers `?tainted string`,
// so a `tainted string` is one narrowing away and never the thing that was returned.
// A reader that answered `T` would compile here and fail on the first NULL.
foreach ($all as Core\Db\Row $named) {
    tainted string $unwrapped = $named->string("owner");
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `tainted string`, found `null|tainted string`
   --> case.nvs:50:33
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
